Gears of War 3: gow2_hud_separate. The upscaler takes the frame as it was before the HUD: the
first draw into the render target of the game's last full-screen pass (gow2_hud_final_ps; Gears 3:
2F284B68A112ED3E, the combined post-process and colour grading pass) gets the target copied first
(render size, through the render target cache's state tracking). The copy is converted like the
frame's resolve to the screen (red/blue swap, exponent bias) so it matches the frame outside the HUD.
The writeback adds the HUD (the game's frame minus the copy, zero outside the HUD) on top of the
upscaled image; opaque HUD pixels are the game's own. Frames without the copy (no HUD, ROV, MSAA)
keep the gow2_ui_mask path. Logs which path frames take every 600 frames.

